      "markup": "d5b2eb12918ffddd4263fc6e0ae87c3d2126de009449b33503df3926f832f86f",
      "mounts": [
        {
          "content": {
            "kind": "markdown",
            "md": "## What the section can do that the document could not\n\nA section is a div. It is full width, it owns its layout entirely, and the reading measure\nlives inside the default section's own file rather than on the sheet — so a band that goes\nedge to edge costs nothing, and a column that wants 34rem of measure asks for it here.\n\n> Prose still wants a measure. A page that is edge to edge everywhere is exactly as\n> monotonous as one that is 34rem everywhere.\n\nThe freedom is to choose per section. Two columns where a figure earns its place beside the\nargument; one column where the words are the whole of it; a grid where things are being\ncompared. A page that chooses the same shape every time has not used any of it.\n\nSwap this slot's prose for the real argument, and swap `kpiName`, `kpiValue`, `barName` and\n`barValue` for the real figures. The tallest bar lights itself, so nothing here has to be\ntold which one matters.\n",
            "vars": {
              "barName": [
                "Feb",
                "Mar",
                "Apr",
                "May",
                "Jun"
              ],
              "barValue": [
                12,
                19,
                34,
                26,
                15
              ],
              "kpiName": [
                "Trays potted on",
                "Trays lost",
                "Trays given away"
              ],
              "kpiValue": [
                17,
                4,
                9
              ]
            }
          },
